.TH CVECTOR_SORT_WITH_COMPARISON_PROC 3 "2026-09-28" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvector_sort_with_comparison_proc \- sort vector with custom comparison
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

cvector_sort_with_comparison_proc(v, comparison_proc);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Sorts the vector in place through the csort library with a custom
comparison function, which must obey the standard comparator convention
of returning a value <0, a value 0, or a value >0.

This macro is the supported way to sort a vector whose element type has
no default comparison procedure, that is, the element types that
cvec_sort refuses to compile: bool, a struct, a union, a pointer to
anything other than char, and a fixed-size char array. This macro also
sorts a type that does have a default comparison procedure, in which case
the given comparison procedure defines the order.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v                 Vector to sort. The macro evaluates it exactly once.
comparison_proc   Comparison function for sorting. The macro evaluates it
                  exactly once.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
Sorts in place with a stable mergesort algorithm
O(n log n) time complexity, O(n) space complexity
Asserts if v is NULL
Uses the stable mergesort of csort, and moves the elements inside the
backing array directly, with no call for each element access
Calls ccol_fatal_err() if comparison_proc is NULL. A comparison procedure
comes here from the caller's own expression, whose value is in general
not known before the program runs, so this check is a run-time check.
The element-type check of cvec_sort is a compile-time _Static_assert
instead, and a cvec_sort call never reaches this diagnostic
Calls ccol_fatal_err() if the allocation of the internal temporary buffer
of the sort fails, as every other type-inferred macro in cvector.h that
changes a vector does (cvec_push, cvec_reserve, cvec_append_array and
the others). The vector stays completely unsorted in that case
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
int compare_ints(const void *a, const void *b) {
  int x = *(const int *)a, y = *(const int *)b;
  return (x > y) - (x < y);
}
cvec_construct(vec, int);
// ... add elements ...
cvector_sort_with_comparison_proc(vec, compare_ints);
cvec_destroy(vec);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvec_sort (3),
.BR csort_sort (3)
